                                </Style>
                            </ContentControl.Style>
                        </ContentControl>
                        <!-- PLAY/PAUSE, added 2026-08-26 on request. The row was
                             STOP-only because letting go of the file is half of
                             what it is for (see the note above the stop button),
                             and that reason has not changed - so this is a
                             SECOND button rather than a replacement, and the way
                             out is still there beside it.
                             The transport's own handler, not a copy: pause and
                             resume already exist, and a second idea of what the
                             button does is how the two would drift apart. Same
                             two glyphs for the same reason; SetViewerVideoPlaying
                             swaps this pair with the transport's own. -->
                        <Button x:Name="FooterNowPlayingPlayPause"
